{"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:15GraphOperations12SubgraphViewV","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"GraphOperations"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SubgraphView.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView.swift#L31"},"symbolKind":"struct","title":"SubgraphView"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations"]]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The kept vertices appear in the base’s order at view indices "},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The view keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two arrays, base index to view index and back, so a row is the base’s row filtered and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"renumbered with one array load per entry. A spanning subgraph keeps every vertex at its base"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Edges keep the base’s positions, so a weight closure keyed by the base’s positions works on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the view. An edge is in the view when both its ends are and, if an edge set was given, when it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is in the set. With an edge set the view has dense edge indices, an edge’s index being its rank","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"among the kept edges in base order. Over a base with edge indices the set is a bit mask with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"count per 64-bit word, and a rank costs one popcount. Over a base without them (an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyMatrix"},{"text":", a complement, an induced subgraph) the set is the sorted kept positions, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a row entry or a rank costs a binary search. An induced subgraph has no edge indices, except one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that keeps every vertex, which keeps the base’s rows and edge indices.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The view holds a copy of the base, so mutating the original doesn’t show through. The base","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"must have vertex indices; construction traps when ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GraphAdaptor"},{"type":"text","text":", its generation is the base’s, and it reads the base’s attached maps."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[map, of: vertex]"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[map, ofEdgeAt: position]"},{"type":"text","text":" trap for a vertex or an edge the view drops,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and their "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checked:"},{"type":"text","text":" forms throw. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the base’s, by the base’s positions. An"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithm on the view reads it only at the kept edges."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"densely. Made by "},{"code":"inducedSubgraphView(on:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"spanningSubgraphView(edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"subgraphView(vertices:edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphAdaptor","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview"]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges"],"anchor":"Structures","generated":true},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gra